auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Kempen Cricket Club — Form APIs

  Azure Functions v4 form endpoints, protected by a shared-secret HS256 JWT.

  ## How auth works
  1. Run **Get Token** — it POSTs the client credentials to `/api/token` and, in a
     post-response script, saves the returned JWT into the `token` environment variable.
  2. Every other request inherits collection-level Bearer auth using `{{token}}`.
  3. When the token expires (default 15m), run **Get Token** again.

  ## Variables
  Select the **Local** environment (or create your own) and set `baseUrl`, `clientUser`,
  `clientPass`. `token` is populated automatically.

  ## Notes
  - **Captcha:** requests send an empty `turnstileToken`. The API skips Cloudflare
    Turnstile verification when `TURNSTILE_SECRET` is unset (typical for local testing).
  - **Duplicate emails:** Join, Register, Subscribe and Contact now reject an email
    that already exists (HTTP 409), so change the `email` in the body between runs
    or the second call will fail the 200 assertion.
}
